{
  "subtitle": "The map-model (RSSM-2) family and the plain baselines: 1.1M env steps each, size50m, scored on the same 30 fixed worlds with tools/death_eval.py. Rows with several training seeds show seed 0. Updated 2026-11-08.",
  "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over 30 evaluation episodes, ± its standard error over those worlds; unlock rates are the share of episodes in which an achievement fired; return is the mean raw Craftax return as a % of the maximum (226). Every checkpoint is scored on the same fixed worlds (env.reseed, audit B05), so comparisons are paired world by world. The error bars cover the worlds only, not training seeds, and one 30-world score moves by about ±0.55 between world sets: a gap under ~1.1 between two single runs is not evidence.\nNo run here uses the rule mask or any other game rule fed to the agent. The map targets (map runs) and the tech-tree potential (potential runs) are hand-built from game knowledge at training time only; the memory target (abl_rssm2) uses none.\nBest scores: the honest map (observation-only targets, potential shaping) 6.17 ± 0.34 on the old code and 5.70 ± 0.21 rerun on the fixed code; the privileged-map control also 6.17 ± 0.23. On the fixed code the honest map leads vanilla DreamerV3 by +1.07 ± 0.24 (paired), though that run also has the potential shaping. RSSM-2 as a memory alone (abl_rssm2) scores 5.33 ± 0.22, +0.57 ± 0.31 over plain (+0.57 ± 0.26 against plain's two seeds): not established, and it trains slightly below plain (5.18 vs 5.43 over the last 100k steps).\nWAKE_UP (sleeping through the night) is a large share of every recent score, plain included (97% of plain's episodes, none of old vanilla's). Without it: vanilla 4.63, plain 3.80, map alone 4.16, honest map 5.20, its fixed rerun 5.17, abl_rssm2 4.33. Among the map runs the potential raises the wood pickaxe from 10% of episodes (map alone) to 33-40% (map + potential, honest map); vanilla made it in 23%, plain in 3%. Normalized return: 2.33% for the honest map, 2.12% for its fixed rerun, 1.96% for abl_rssm2, 1.71% for plain and 1.65% for vanilla.",
  "table_note": "ach. ± SE = mean episode-final achievements ± standard error over the 30 worlds (one training seed). w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. return = raw Craftax return, % of 226. Rates are % of episodes. Vanilla: the original September checkpoint. Plain (new code): main's code. Map rows before honest map fix ran on code older than the 2026-10-11 RSSM-2 fixes (docs/rssm2-step-alignment.md); they are the original checkpoints, re-scored. 'bug' = imag_shift True (the crop slides through imagination; broken, fixed 2026-09-20). map: RSSM-2 trained on a coarse map of the level, read by the actor and critic. 5 hand rewards: survival 'shaped'. potential: survival 'potential' (tech-tree spine). Privileged map: targets from the true map on every cell (the old runs' targets), with the recipe and death fixes to the potential. Honest map: targets only from what the agent observed, with hindsight. Plain + RSSM-2: RSSM-2 as a memory (no map labels), no shaping.",
